---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { buyerContext, tiers, proof } from "../data/site.js";
---
<Base title="About — Anvi Innovate"
  description="Anvi Innovate supplies Forward Deployed AI Engineers and assessed early-career engineers to teams building production AI across India.">
  <span class="pill">About</span>
  <h1>Production AI needs engineers who have seen it break</h1>
  <div style="max-width:780px;">
    <p class="muted" style="font-size:1.1rem;">
      Anvi Innovate supplies the engineers who take AI systems from a working demo to something a
      business can actually depend on. We train them on documented production failures, assess them
      against that, and place them inside client teams.
    </p>

    <h2>The model</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      Two tiers, named honestly. <strong>{tiers[0].name}</strong> are experienced, AI-native engineers who
      own a system end to end — roughly half full-stack systems work, a third applied AI, and the rest
      advising the client. <strong>{tiers[1].name}</strong> are graduates and career-switchers who have
      completed the same curriculum and passed the same assessment, deployed in a pod under an FDE rather
      than dropped into a team alone.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      You interview every person before they start. We do not place anyone you have not met.
    </p>

    <h2>Why this, and why now</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      Global capability centres have become the dominant buyer of contract engineering talent in India —
      <strong>{buyerContext.gccShare}</strong> of professional staffing headcount at the market leader
      ({buyerContext.gccSrc}). Their constraint is not headcount. It is finding engineers who can be
      trusted with a retrieval system, an agent or an evaluation harness in front of real users.
      Most training stops at the tutorial. Ours starts at the incident report.
    </p>

    <h2>How the training is built</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      The curriculum is assembled from <strong>{proof.caseStudies} verified production case studies</strong>
      across <strong>{proof.organisations} companies</strong> — engineering blogs, published postmortems,
      applied research and regulatory findings. Every case was retrieved from a primary source and
      fact-checked before it was taught, and each one names what the team tried first, what regressed and
      what it cost. Engineers work <strong>{proof.scenarios} mandatory hands-on scenarios</strong> drawn
      from those failures before they are put in front of a client.
    </p>

    <h2>Where we work</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      We work with teams across India — product companies, enterprises and the global capability centres
      building their AI capacity here — and we support engagements outside India where the delivery model fits.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
